cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata (and the accompanying paper, Ravoux et al. 2025)."
title: flip
abstract: >-
  Field-level inference of the growth rate of structure from the peculiar
  velocity and density fields by maximum likelihood. flip builds a covariance
  matrix from a model power spectrum and the survey coordinates (generalised to
  any linear velocity / density / cross power-spectrum model and optimised with
  Hankel transforms), turns it into a likelihood, and fits the growth rate with
  Minuit or MCMC (emcee).
type: software
